WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.560
Hello, my name is Taha Jaid, SOC Manager at AMANDIGITAL,

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.540
a provider of managed SOC services (MSSP).

3
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.360
About your topic: at AMANDIGITAL, since I started,

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.980
where I’m now SOC Manager,

5
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:22.000
I handle all the architecture and configuration of our SOC.

6
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:26.320
I’ve had the chance to take part in recruiting young cybersecurity profiles,

7
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.700
especially final-year interns, and even end-of-year interns.

8
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:35.680
What I learned from this is that a candidate who aces the interview

9
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.520
is not necessarily the one who will be the most competent in the field.

10
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.200
Some are very at ease speaking,

11
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.900
while others are more reserved because of stress.

12
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.020
Personally, I don’t see nervousness as a lack of skills.

13
00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.740
What interests me above all is their ability to think, to analyse a problem

14
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.620
and to explain their reasoning.

15
00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.620
And especially, if they are engineering students,

16
00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:07.640
do they think like an engineer, who is supposed to find solutions to problems?

17
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.040
Because I don’t rely much on the technical level;

18
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.040
above all, I look at how they think, how they reason.

19
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.260
For example, in our field, cybersecurity,

20
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:22.860
I like to present a concrete situation, like a suspicious security alert,

21
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:27.660
and ask the candidate how they would investigate and handle it.

22
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:31.040
I’m not necessarily looking for a perfect answer.

23
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.460
Above all, I want to understand their logic, their curiosity, their ability to learn.

24
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:42.160
And if the alert or the problem was really complicated for them,

25
00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:46.500
I’d like to see that they never give up.

26
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.980
Because in our field, cybersecurity,

27
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.300
if you give up, you just stop and jump to another problem

28
00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.860
because it’s too complicated.

29
00:01:54.900 --> 00:02:00.300
There are fewer resources online, especially for solving problems or alerts.

30
00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.820
And of course, technical knowledge matters too,

31
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:08.880
but motivation, an analytical mind and the will to improve matter just as much.

32
00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:13.020
For me, a recruiter’s role is to give every candidate

33
00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:19.350
a real chance to show their potential, without stopping at the first impression.
